\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:Copper Could Correct, Then Rise Into Year End - DB\b0\par\par\uc2 1,581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 04:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0246 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says copper prices being driven by macroeconomic factors rather than physical dynamics, noting 8% increase in copper inventory at Shanghai Futures Exchange over past week ignored. "While we expect that there could be a near-term pullback in prices after the strong rally over the past month, we expect that prices could continue higher into the New Year as the effects of QE keep industrial demand supported and investment demand potential grows as a driver." FOMC meeting minutes at 1800 GMT likely to be watched for further indications on quantitative easing. LME 3-month copper at $8,250/ton, down $35 with 1,043 lots done. (james.campbell@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0234 GMT [Dow Jones] Standard Chartered Bank recommends taking profit on short USD/PHP via 3-month NDFs, with outright exit rate pegged at 43.77; "technicals, positioning and declining risk appetite suggest that USD/PHP may correct higher...fundamentally, we like this trade and will look to re-enter at better levels." Fundamentally, Standard Chartered has \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating of Overweight on PHP on growth. Spot last at 43.62. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0233 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei off 0.9% at 9504.39 midday with investor sentiment soured by firmer yen (USD/JPY at 82.09) vs Friday, and surprise FY profit forecast cut by \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  (9983.TO); decline in Chinese shares also weighing on market following Reuters report that reserve requirements on 6 big banks temporarily raised to drain 