\par\par \b \uc2 PRECIOUS METALS: Gold Up In Asia; Silver Off Early High\b0\par\par\uc2 By James Campbell  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2010\par 09:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Gold and silver shot out of the blocks in Asia Monday, building on Friday's gains after weak U.S. employment data increased the attractiveness of precious metals as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedge.\par \par \uc2 The data, which were far worse than expected, make it more likely that the U.S. Federal Reserve will restart its quantitative easing program at its next meeting, although St. Louis Fed President James Bullard said Friday that any decision by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers on more asset purchases will be difficult as chances of a double-dip recession have receded.\par \par \uc2 Silver hit a new 30-year high of $23.64 a troy ounce, before paring some of its gains, while gold moved back above $1,350/oz.\par \par \uc2 "After having undergone a severe correction on Thursday we would define the market as much healthier now," MKS Finance said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The gains were helped by action in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, where the dollar continued to struggle against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro flirted with $1.40 and the dollar hit a 15-year low against the yen at Y81.37 in early trade, despite the prospect of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0630 GMT, spot gold was at $1,353/oz, up $6, while spot silver was at $23.39/oz, up 17 cents. The Tokyo Commodity Exchange was closed for a national holiday.\par \par \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said a combination of factors driving gold recently--including speculation over Fed policy and de-hedging by producers--could have largely dissipated by November, when seasonal strength typically starts to fade.\par \par \uc2 "Beyond the seasonally strong period, the (Federal Open Market Committee) meeting in November and given the completion of the announced hedgebook buybacks, we would not rule out prices correcting," it said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Platinum and palladium were higher, helped by rallying industrial metals and broadly firm equity markets.\par \par \uc2 Spot platinum was at $1,702/oz, up $1, while palladium was $5 higher at $589/oz.\par \par \uc2 -By James Campbell, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-082; james.campbell@dowjones.com [ 11-10-10 0708GMT ]\par \par \uc2 70576 82139  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101011e6ab000g8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
