inc gained $40 at $2,330. (ray.brindal@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2239 GMT [Dow Jones] Australian financial markets have placed 50/50 bets on an RBA rate hike at November policy meeting, according to analysis by \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . Lack of certainty in markets likely reflects surprise decision by RBA in October to hold rates steady at 4.50%. Despite recent hawkish rhetoric from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , markets only expect two 25 bps rate hikes over the next two years, CS report shows. (james.glynn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2224 GMT [Dow Jones] Despite offshore macro headwinds, Australian corporate earnings risk remains skewed to the upside, particularly in light of strong domestic macro environment, featuring strong employment, record trade surplus and double-digit nominal GDP growth, says \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 . "Historically, increases to year-on-year GDP growth of greater than 150 basis points, particularly following a large earnings decline, have been consistent with double-digit Industrials EPS growth," says broker. Expects key themes from upcoming AGM season to include appreciating Australian dollar, increasing cost pressures and commodity prices, accelerating domestic economy, weakening developed-market economies and balance sheet strength/capital deployment. S&P/ASX 200 last 4697.5. (david.rogers1@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2213 GMT [Dow Jones] Spot gold $1,355.30/oz, up $1.40 from late NY, just shy of yesterday's intraday high of $1,355.50. ScotiaMocatta says there are no reversal signals on charts so bias remains for another push higher, with important supports pegged at $1,320, then $1,312. (ray.brindal@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2205 GMT [Dow Jones] S&P/ASX 200 offshore leads mostly flat, with overnight SPI 200 futures up 3 points at 4718.0 after basically steady night in offshore markets, with U.S. bond market, government offices closed for Columbus Day. DJIA flat at 11010.11, S&P 500 flat at 1165.30, Nasdaq flat at 2402.33. CBOE VIX fell 8.5% to 18.96. OECD leading economic indicators pointed to global slowdown. NABE survey showed economists expect U.S. GDP to rise 2.6% this year and next. Kansas Fed's Hoenig said sustained low interest rates will create new imbalances, possibly causing inflation and be harmful to economic recovery. S&P 500 Financials down 0.1%. S&P 500 Materials down 0.1, with \uc2 Alcoa\uc2  up 0.3%, Vale up 1.0%, Freeport down 0.1%, \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  down 0.7%, Barrick Gold up 0.3%. BHP ADRs at A$41.20 vs local close at A$41.45. London listed BHP down 0.5%, Rio (RIO.AU) down 1.1%. S&P 500 Industrials down 0.3%. S&P 500 Energy up 0.2%. S&P 500 Consumer Discretionary up 0.1%. Spot gold at US$1,353.65 vs US$1,3486.0. Nymex crude oil down 0.5% at US$82.21. LME copper down 0.3%, zinc up 1.9%, aluminum down 0.8%, nickel down 0.2%. In \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, EUR/USD at 1.3876 vs 1.3992. AUD/USD at 0.9834 vs 0.9894. S&P/ASX 200 last 4697.5. (david.rogers1@dowjones.com) [ 10-11-10 1936ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101011e6ab000bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
