\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: High Probability Of Japan Policy Failure\b0\par\par\uc2 1,237 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2010\par 09:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0744 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy may be increasing speculation, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The bank reckons that the BOJ's inactivity while USD/JPY has fallen under 83 level that triggered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in mid-September suggests the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is pursuing a "leaning against the wind" policy rather than defending a line in the sand. "The strategy of leaning against the wind might fuel the JPY appreciation pressure it is trying to dampen," the bank says, noting that the probability of such a policy failing is high. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0744 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/THB expected to consolidate near 30.00 level near term but could slip to 28 or 29 if yuan stronger. "Now that the Thai baht has outperformed the regional peers (second strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region after yen), the pace of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation is likely to slow down," says \uc2 Siam Commercial Bank\uc2 's Senior Executive Vice President Arthid Nanthawithaya. Says USD still in bearish-mode. Notes local newspaper report saying Thai Finance Ministry plans to impose 15% tax on interest, capital gains unlikely to have significant impact to stop capital inflows as foreign investors booking gains from \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bond, stock markets worth more than tax charged. Arthid says BOT could inject USD in market to help balance dollar demand, supply. "There are companies that need some funds in dollar denominated terms...We have projects like power generating business that needs the loans in dollar term," says Arthid. USD/THB last 30.04-30.06 vs 30.00 early. (piyarat.setthasiriphaiboon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0738 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/SEK will trade lower today as bearish signals from Friday point to further downside action, says SEB. "We are thus looking for a break of 9.2550 to push the pair down into the next support, 9.2155/2230," the bank adds. EUR/SEK trades at 9.2520. (charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0737 GMT [Dow Jones] October HSI futures +1.5% at 23,243, rising more than cash market +1.3% in thrusting to more than 2-year high. Contract continues to defy profit-taking pressure, trading at premium to cash most of time, even with HK market rising for 23rd session out of past 27, although it's likely matter of time before index retreats to correct overbought conditions. Volume modest at 55,163 lots. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0737 GMT [Dow Jones] China government bonds end lower on concerns of monetary tightening. Shanghai Exchange government bond index ends at 126.66 vs intraday high of 126.75, Friday's 126.70; support tipped at 126.60. "With expectations of rising inflationary pressure, the bond market will likely continue to correct in the short term," says Shanghai-based trader at local bank. Still, if \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intends to keep liquidity ample, downside will be limited. This week, CNY295 billion worth of bills and repurchase agreements will mature. 20-year bond issued in 2001 traded actively, ending at CNY106.64 vs CNY107.15 Friday, with yield of 3.5155% vs 3.4607%. (rose.yu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0731 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are down Monday, falling in line with bunds as firm stocks spur traders to book some profits. A weaker-than-expected US nonfarm payrolls report on Friday strengthened calls for the Fed to announce additional asset purchases to support the economy, helping other core government bonds as well. Talk of the BOE possibly following the Fed in buying more government bonds has also risen, and BOE minutes due later this month may show a 3-way split in voting. The economic calendar is thin, although CPI figures are due on Tuesday. December gilts are down 0.21 at 125.16 and the 10-year gilt is down at 115.364 to yield 2.874%.(neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0730 GMT [Dow Jones] Aggregate net USD positions fell to nearly an all-time low, according to Credit Agricole's summary of the latest speculative data from the Chicago Mercantile Exchange. However, positioning in the EUR is well below its all-time highs. This, the bank says, supports "the view that rather than speculative investors, it is central banks that are pushing the EUR higher." (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0730 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia government bonds tad lower late as investors lock in profit on report Thai MOF may propose to Cabinet plan to impose 15% withholding tax on interest, capital gains on bond transactions as part of package measures to curb THB's rise, says dealer with local bank. "Though Malaysia is unlikely to follow Thailand's lead, people are naturally cautious and prefer to book in some profit," says dealer. Adds, market largely unmoved by Malaysia's August industrial output data (+0.4% on-year vs +0.5% tipped by Dow Jones). Tips bonds to stay in tight range Tuesday in absence of major market moving news. Yields on August 2015 MGS flat at 3.25%, September MGS 2017 +1 bp at 3.56% and November 2019 MGS +2 bps at 3.67%. (elffie.chew@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0729 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY has recovered from a test and break of its 5-month support line at 81.62. However, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 's Axel Rudolph expects this to fail along with the 5-year support line at 80.40 and result in a test of the 79.90 all-time lows. Topside Rudolph says resistance comes in at 84.03, 84.49 and 84.86 and only above the latter will signal a reversal is underway. USD/JPY now trades at 82.01. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0724 GMT [Dow Jones] Friday's disappointing U.S. payrolls and no agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues from the weekend's IMF meeting leaves the dollar under pressure, with AUD, the euro and JPY especially in demand. USD/JPY fell to a new 15-year low of 81.37 in Asia Monday despite the door to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  being left open after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  received no official criticism at the weekend's gathering for its September 15 foray into the markets. For Monday there is no first tier data on offer and with both Japan and U.S. markets on holiday \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  action is likely to be thin and choppy. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0718 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP turns higher as some foreign banks buy; pair last at 43.53 in heavy volume vs 43.32 earlier, 43.435 late Friday; support tipped at 43.30, resistance at 43.60. "Some banks are trimming dollar-shorts, taking profit," says local bank trader. "We also saw profit-taking in the stock market."(cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0717 GMT [Dow Jones] With the IMF failing to increase \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  coordination and with the U.S. and China unlikely to cut a deal on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the G20 leaders summit meeting in South Korea in November, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are likely to see intensification of current trends, says Bank of New York Mellon. "Heightened USD weakness, increased capital flows into emerging markets, increased \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (possibly from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well) and diversification will be the order of the day," the bank warns. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com) [ 10-11-10 0344ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101011e6ab0004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
