\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: ECB's Draghi Criticizes Japan's Move To Weaken Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2010\par 18:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with additional details and background.)\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Mario Draghi Sunday criticized Japan's recent move to weaken the yen, saying it showed that unilateral action in world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is not effective.\par \par \uc2 Draghi told a press conference held after the International Monetary Fund and World Bank annual meetings that countries should refrain from manipulating their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to solve the current "misalignments" in world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels.\par \par \uc2 The IMF meetings have so far failed to ease \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  battles currently roiling markets, in which several big economies including Japan and China are explicitly trying to lift their economies by keeping their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weak to boost exports.\par \par \uc2 In an effort to jump-start its stagnant economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets last month to tame the yen's continued rise, but the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still surged Friday to a 15-year high above Y81.7 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Not only is it against the spirit we ought to have--it also doesn't yield results," Draghi told reporters when asked specifically about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite some recent tensions, Draghi said no "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars" are taking place and expressed confidence that problems would be solved. The Bank of Italy governor, who also heads a global panel of financial regulators, said international cooperation is much better now compared with the trade wars that followed the Wall Street crash in 1929, when the IMF didn't exist.\par \par \uc2 Still, the IMF meetings have failed to come up with concrete results, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dispute off to a summit next month of leaders of Group of 20 countries, with no clear resolution in sight. Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials rejected calls for an international or regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accord, and the World Trade Organization's chief said his institution didn't want to get involved in exchange-rate fights. IMF members also scotched an effort by the U.S. to link a bigger Chinese role in the IMF to changes in Beijing's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the high level of the euro, which is likely to hurt the 16-country area by hitting exports, Draghi declined to give a direct comment. He said the ECB's mandate is to keep inflation in check, indicating there's little the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can do given that a high euro actually helps to keep prices in check. Unlike other central banks like the Federal Reserve, the ECB doesn't have a second task of stimulating the economy and employment.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the euro climbed to a eight-month high against the U.S. dollar, briefly topping $1.40. Part of the rise, analysts say, is due to signals from the ECB that it in unlikely to embark on aggressive new steps to boost economic activity, in contrast to the Fed and Bank of England, where officials are considering new rounds of large-scale asset purchases known as quantitative easing, and the Bank of Japan, which has already announced plans to buy assets.\par \par \uc2 -By Luca Di Leo, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-862-6682; luca.dileo@@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (Brian Blackstone and Bob Davis contributed to this article.) [ 10-10-10 1249ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101010e6aa0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
