\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Dollar selling likely to continue after IMF meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven C. Johnson  \par \uc2 905 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2010\par 21:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Oct 10 (Reuters) - Investors will keep on selling the U.S. dollar and chasing higher returns in emerging markets after finance leaders this weekend produced no quick fix for uneven global growth and tensions in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Markets will also be on alert for more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold yen on the open market last month for the first time since 2004 in order to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar and support Japan's export-driven economy.\par \par \uc2 Super-loose U.S. monetary policy, and the prospect of more easing, has helped pushed the dollar to an 8-1/2-month low and diverted funds into higher-yielding emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 To stop their economies from overheating and defend their exporters, some emerging governments have moved to stem the rise of their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sparking talk of a brewing "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war." China, in particular, has refused U.S. and European entreaties to let the yuan appreciate more rapidly.\par \par \uc2 With only a vague plan to monitor large countries' economic policies more closely, the weekend International Monetary Fund meeting ended without concrete action on exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the way is now clear for the U.S. Federal Reserve to resort to even more stimulus next month. It is expected to pump more money into the economy through the purchase of U.S. government bonds and possibly mortgage-backed debt -- which would weaken the dollar even further.\par \par \uc2 "Overall, despite occasional reference to a strong dollar policy -- which increasingly sounds anachronistic -- there is little to suggest that the dollar's direction is anything but down," said Steven Englander, \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's director of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy.\par \par \uc2 That was likely not lost on European policymakers, who fear a stronger euro will hurt growth in the 16-nation euro zone. As European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said over the weekend: "The U.S. authorities, to my knowledge, are in favor of a strong dollar, and you know I appreciate always this reference."\par \par \uc2 Market analysts at IFR (a unit of Thomson Reuters) said traders' initial reaction will likely be to buy the euro and commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Australian dollar when trading resumes on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Both the euro and Aussie have soared against the greenback of late, with the euro hitting an 8-1/2-month high above $1.40 <EUR=> and the Australian dollar a two-year peak less than 2 cents away from parity.\par \par \uc2 With positions against the dollar already stretched, \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  strategist Marc Chandler said a respite was possible in the days ahead. Monday's trading was likely to be light due to holidays in Japan and the United States.\par \par \uc2 But technical strategists said support will likely keep the euro above $1.35 in the medium term, particularly with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to embrace tighter monetary policy more quickly than the Fed.\par \par \uc2 DISCORD GROWS,\par \par \uc2 The discord among global policymakers over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue has been striking.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has doubled a tax on foreign purchases of local bonds. South Korea has warned of new trading limits, and India has said it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 China has reaffirmed plans to allow eventual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, but at its own pace.\par \par \uc2 "That there seems to be lack of agreement as to what needs to be done at the global level with the major economies is of concern to us," said Thailand's finance minister, Korn Chatikavanij, at the IMF meeting. "There seems to be a race to the bottom...and that's very problematic."\par \par \uc2 Alan Ruskin, the head of \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's global G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, said the trend in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the logical consequence of divergent economic trends, and in the long run is necessary to smooth out imbalances in the global economy.\par \par \uc2 "This is about much more than the Fed getting ready to launch more quantitative easing," he said. "We've had low interest rates in the most developed economies for some time and we have robust growth and the need to tighten policy elsewhere. That suggests the flows going into the emerging world are going to continue."\par \par \uc2 JAPAN'S FREE PASS\par \par \uc2 Trading the yen could be tricker. While traders may try to test the Bank of Japan's resolve by pushing the dollar toward a record low, analysts said risks remain.\par \par \uc2 Some said U.S. silence over the weekend about the yen may be seen as tacit approval for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. The dollar fell to a 15-year low beneath 82 yen <JPY=> on Friday, below its trading level when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sept 15.\par \par \uc2 "Geithner was pretty easy on the Japanese so there might be people getting afraid that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again," Chandler said, referring to U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner. He added that some traders may opt to scale back short dollar/yen and euro/yen trades.\par \par \uc2 Ruskin said Japan probably earned a free pass for now because it was trying to slow rapid yen appreciation rather than targeting a level as some emerging market countries do.\par \par \uc2 "I think the U.S. wants to avoid Japan becoming a distraction from efforts to get more Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility." (Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /IMF (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|Z|J|UKI  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101013e6aa001ce\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
