\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Steps countries are taking to counter hot money\b0\par\par\uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2010\par 19:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Oct 10 (Reuters) - More governments around the world are moving to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating as investors, turning their backs on low interest rates in developed economies, pour money into higher-yielding markets.\par \par \uc2 Rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions were discussed by finance ministers at the International Monetary Fund at its twice-yearly gathering this weekend. [ID:nN09263971]\par \par \uc2 Below are recent cases of direct or indirect government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, compiled by Reuters:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  CUTS RATES, \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOR FIRST TIME SINCE 2004\par \par \uc2 * Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  unexpectedly pledges to pump more funds into the economy on Oct 5, launches "comprehensive monetary easing," cuts rates to virtually zero.\par \par \uc2 * Authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Sept. 15, first time since 2004, to drive down yen, selling estimated 2 trillion yen. Figures later show September sales total 2.1249 trillion yen ($25.37 billion)\par \par \uc2 * Prime minister signals Tokyo ready to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says United States did not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at meeting in Washington on Oct 9 [ID:nTOE69801I]\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL TAKES MORE AGGRESSIVE ACTION\par \par \uc2 * Brazil warns of "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war"\par \par \uc2 * Government doubles tax on foreigners buying local bonds\par \par \uc2 * Brazil sovereign fund yet to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps up daily dollar auctions\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nN05219921] [ID:nN04132890] [ID:nN20102448] [ID:nN23213114]\par \par \uc2 SWITZERLAND HOLDS OFF ON \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank spent nearly 200 billion Swiss francs via \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from March 2009\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped in June of this year\par \par \uc2 * Traders speculate \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  move could prompt SNB to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Swiss franc flirting with parity against dollar\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nLDE68D1IK]\par \par \uc2 CHILE WARNS ON PESO, NO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  YET\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says no plans for capital controls\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief says weighing peso \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues threats but reluctant to act\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID:nN08249033] [ID:nN06248445]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA WARNS OF NEW LIMITS\par \par \uc2 * Government warns of new limits on forwards\par \par \uc2 * Regulator asks banks not to lend in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Authorities repeatedly spotted buying dollars to curb the pace of appreciation in the won.\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose more than $4 billion in September to a record level of $290 billion.\par \par \uc2 -- Story links: [ID: