\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:G-7 Agrees Developing Nations Need Flexible  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  - Japan Noda\b0\par\par\uc2 781 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2010\par 09:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with more comments from Japan's finance minister on the G-7 dinner meeting, more background.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--Group of Seven industrial powers agreed Friday that developing nations running trade surpluses must make their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  more flexible, Japan's finance minister said, a move likely designed to apply further pressure on China.\par \par \uc2 But finance chiefs from the G-7 leading countries had no debates over \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's controversial market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted last month to tame the yen's continued rise, leaving it unclear whether they endorse the Japanese action, Yoshihiko Noda said.\par \par \uc2 During a dinner meeting of G-7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors, "we agreed that emerging, surplus nations should boost the flexibility of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Noda said at a news conference. "We also confirmed ... that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates contribute to the stability of the world economy if they reflect the fundamentals of their underlying economies and are being set in the market."\par \par \uc2 The move adds to signs that advanced countries are turning up the heat on China to loosen its grip on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan. The U.S. and Europe are increasingly frustrated with Beijing's policy of keeping the yuan weak enough to boost Chinese exports at the expense of overseas producers, despite China's now being the world's second largest economy.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices have also fueled concern that they might spur what some call a global "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war." It refers to a competition by authorities to weaken their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift exports, a process many say would end up damaging economies around the world. But Noda said "there were no debates in terms of a competition to devalue \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " Friday.\par \par \uc2 Whether the G-7's efforts will bear fruit is far from certain.\par \par \uc2 Asia's biggest economy in mid-June ended a two-year peg of the yuan to the dollar, but has since let its tightly managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise just around 2%. Friday, People's Bank of China Gov. Zhou Xiaochaun played down the foreign criticism, saying international calls for a quicker yuan ascent would fade if developed economies recover.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, officials from the G-7--the U.S., Japan, Germany, France, the U.K., Italy and Canada--reaffirmed their well-worn principle that excessive or disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves are not welcome, Noda said. They also agreed that exchange rates should mirror the strength of their underlying economies, and that the group will "cooperate as appropriate" on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 How the G-7 views \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move in September to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in more than six years to slow the yen's advance remain unclear.\par \par \uc2 "Our nation's economy is still in a severe situation with deflation continuing, and under this circumstance, excessive fluctuations in exchange rates have an negative impact on Japan's economy and thus can't be overlooked," Noda said, as he explained the remarks he made to his G-7 counterparts. "I explained to them that we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the purpose of curbing excessive volatility. Our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't the kind of long-term, large-scale campaign that aimed to bring (the yen) to certain levels."\par \par \uc2 But "this didn't lead to broader debates," as G-7 officials just quietly listened to his speech and showed little reaction, Noda said. "I can't say assertively" that he has gained G-7 support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The finance minister said he didn't explain \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current policy to his G-7 counterparts--the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if necessary. Yet Noda said "I think it was understood that our fundamental stance is the same as theirs."\par \par \uc2 Lack of clarity over the G-7's thinking of Japan's action could make it hard for traders to predict whether and how soon Tokyo may act against the yen, which surged Friday to a 15-year high of 81.72 yen to the dollar. Many had speculated that should the G-7 back Japan's approach, it could embolden the MOF, lifting the odds of Japanese action.\par \par \uc2 Noda said he will convey \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's views on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner in a planned one-on-one meeting Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Noda added that the G-7 agreed to "firmly unite themselves" to deal with issues concerning inflows and outflows of money in the globe and that it discussed the idea of multinational cooperation to fix \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  problems.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 10-09-10 0335ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020101009e6a90000h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
