\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Fin Min: G-7 Reaffirms Stance Vs Excess  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2010\par 06:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--Group of Seven officials reaffirmed Friday that excessive exchange-rate volatility isn't welcome, exchange rates should reflect economic fundamentals, and developing nations with a trade surplus ought to make their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexible, Japan's finance minister said.\par \par \uc2 "One of the things we agreed upon is that excessive fluctuations or disorderly movements in exchange rates are not desirable regarding the stability of economic and financial conditions," Yoshihiko Noda said at a joint news conference with Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa.\par \par \uc2 The two attended a dinner meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from the G-7 leading industrialized nations.\par \par \uc2 Noda added that he had explained to other G-7 officials about the reasons behind \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, but said he couldn't say if he succeeded in gaining their understanding.\par \par \uc2 He said he told the group: "With deflation continuing and the Japanese economy still in a severe situation, excessive volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates can't be overlooked as it could have adverse effects on the stability of Japan's economy." But "this didn't lead to broader debates," and "I can't say assertively" that he has won support from the G-7 for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Noda added that during the G-7 talks, he didn't explain \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance that it will take decisive steps, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when necessary.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2781; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 10-09-10 0002ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020101009e6a90000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
