D/USD aroused from a sleepy pre-weekend session by news \uc2 Moody's\uc2  has China's A1 bond rating on review for a possible upgrade. Pair rises from around 0.9800 to 0.9825 after report. China is Australia's biggest export destination and pair highly sensitive to any reports from Asian giant. Greg Gibbs, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBS, says news likely gave pair a solid boost. Resistance likely around 0.9850, a former long-term record high for pair. All eyes now on imminent speech by RBA Deputy Governor Battellino amid widespread expectations \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise rates at its next policy meeting in November. Pair now 0.9826. (james.glynn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0248 GMT [Dow Jones] India government bonds may open higher on rise in U.S. Treasurys, but likely to give up gains ahead of INR110 billion auction, inflation concerns, says trader with primary dealership. Finance Minister Mukherjee says in Washington yesterday that high inflation continues to be of concern, but he's "more concerned with inflationary pressures on food items." Adds government's measures to open up importing of food items that are in short supply as well as recent interest rate increases by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would bring inflation down to 6% by FY end. Dealer says "the recent comments from RBI also signal that the hiking cycle is not over." But expects bond auction to be fully subscribed, trading interest in 8.13% 2022 paper (which auction bond). RBI to sell INR40 billion of 7.99% 2017 bond, INR40 billion of 8.13% 2022 and INR30 billion of 8.30% 2040. (subhadip.sircar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0247 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares +0.5% at 464.51, with investors buying on hopes that banks will start lowering interest rates from mid-October to boost liquidity, support companies which are facing borrowing rates above 15%; state-run Vietnam Bank Association asks banks to lower intere