\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 3-World finance leaders seek  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  peace\b0\par\par\uc2 894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2010\par 17:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Finance leaders trying to soothe \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions\par \par \uc2 * China lets yuan rise, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  says to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed\par \par \uc2 * Canada says all must live up to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  commitments (Recasts; adds comments from U.S., Brazilian finance officials)\par \par \uc2 By Louise Egan and Glenn Somerville\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Oct 8 (Reuters) - World finance leaders sought on Friday to tamp down simmering \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions that threaten a painfully slow economic recovery, with the United States calling on the IMF to take a stronger hand in bringing about order.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner said the rebalancing of the global economy was not progressing as well as needed, and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in countries with undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were hindering the effort.\par \par \uc2 "It is ultimately the responsibility of countries to act but the IMF must speak out effectively about challenges and marshal support for action," he said.\par \par \uc2 Group of 20 finance ministers met over breakfast to thrash out the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues, which are in the forefront of this weekend's International Monetary Fund and World Bank twice-yearly meetings.\par \par \uc2 Canadian Finance Minister Jim Flaherty told reporters it was vital G20 countries not engage in protectionist measures in an effort to export their way to health, but he also singled out China, saying it must live up to a commitment to allow more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.\par \par \uc2 He expressed hope officials in Washington over the weekend could find a way through the thorny thicket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions that have raised fears of a global round of competitive devaluations.\par \par \uc2 "I would expect that we'd arrive at a consensus with respect to the necessary direction," he said.\par \par \uc2 The smaller group of rich G7 advanced economies was set to hold a closed-door dinner later Friday at which \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also expected to be discussed.\par \par \uc2 China's policy of managing the value of its yuan has raised the hackles of trade partners who consider it unfairly undervalued and who charge it permits China to rack up huge trade surpluses at others' expense.\par \par \uc2 The yuan ended at its highest closing level on Friday since a landmark revaluation in July 2005, possibly a sign Beijing is sensitive to the growing demands to let it rise more rapidly.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve will further ease monetary policy -- bolstered by a report showing the U.S. economy lost 95,000 jobs last month -- has pushed the dollar down to an 8-1/2 month low against a broad basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar's drop has led investors to chase bigger returns in emerging markets such as Brazil, driving up asset prices and inflation.\par \par \uc2 "There are serious \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  imbalances in the world," Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles said.\par \par \uc2 "It has to be addressed. It will certainly be discussed during the IMF meeting here in Washington and certainly also in the G20 summit," he said, referring to an upcoming gathering of world leaders in South Korea.\par \par \uc2 COMING TO THE TABLE?\par \par \uc2 Olli Rehn, the European Union's economic and monetary affairs commissioner, said \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on the table but in the broader context of trying to rebalance global growth to make it more durable.\par \par \uc2 "We are discussing what kind of policy measures are needed to rebalance global growth and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue is certainly one of those," Rehn told reporters.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue is complicated. Some countries, including \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have made clear they reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' values if necessary.\par \par \uc2 "We are approaching a G7 meeting, but regardless of this, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take firm measures, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when needed," Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said.\par \par \uc2 China, usually at the center of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate, has company this time, but \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to weaken the yen put Tokyo on the hot seat, too.\par \par \uc2 The United States can also expect criticism over its seemingly benign neglect of the sinking dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strains are symptomatic of a deeper problem: most advanced economies are not growing rapidly enough to reduce unemployment despite trillions of dollars in government stimulus spending and emergency loan guarantees.\par \par \uc2 For the United States and much of Europe, options for providing more stimulus are limited because either politics, creditors or both prevent them from amassing significantly larger piles of government debt.\par \par \uc2 Until rich nations find their footing, emerging markets will be the strongest source of global growth. So far, they seem to be up to the task. The IMF expects emerging markets to grow at three times the pace of advanced economies next year.\par \par \uc2 Those countries are clamoring for greater decision-making power at the IMF, commensurate with their growing economic prowess. This has been another thorny issue for G7 and G20 leaders who have yet to agree on how exactly to divvy up power when no one wants to relinquish their own position.\par \par \uc2 The United States thinks Europe ought to give up some if its seats on the IMF executive board, while European countries have proposed a seat-sharing rotation. IMF officials are hopeful progress can be made toward resolving reform issues by the time G20 leaders gather in Seoul next month. (Additional reporting by Reuters IMF team; writing by Emily Kaiser and Glenn Somerville, editing by Tim Ahmann)\par \par \uc2 IMF/ (WRAPUP 3) (PIX)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101008e6a80016p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
