\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  COLUMN-Market underestimating potential G7/IMF outcomes\b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2010\par 10:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  -- Rick Lloyd and Krishna Kumar are Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts and John Noonan is head of Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  at IFR Markets. The views expressed are their own --\par \par \uc2  By Rick Lloyd, John Noonan and Krishna Kumar\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE/SYDNEY Oct 8 - Asian central banks, including the People's Bank of China, may be underestimating the frustration within the IMF and Group of Seven about their large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Although the G7 has become something of a toothless tiger of late, market opinion is starting to believe that strong language could emerge on EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from this weekend's meetings or at the upcoming Group of 20 gatherings in South Korea.\par \par \uc2  Pointed comments from the head of the International Monetary Fund on Thursday -- that undervaluation of the yuan is the source of tensions in the world economy, and yuan appreciation is needed to avoid creating the conditions for a new crisis -- underscore this shift in sentiment.\par \par \uc2  So, China may find it more prudent to allow a gradual appreciation of the yuan, rather than face down the G7 or even the entire G20.\par \par \uc2  That would be counter to the prevailing market view that China will soon hit the brakes on yuan appreciation after allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to jump 2 percent in a little more than a month.\par \par \uc2  Further yuan gains would probably give other Asian central banks room to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain because they would not have to worry about sacrificing competitiveness to China.\par \par \uc2  Even in absolute terms, most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are nowhere near their all-time highs.\par \par \uc2  Take the South Korean won <KRW=>. It is not even at the 2010 high reached in April before market players started fretting about a double-dip recession in the United States.\par \par \uc2  In fact, the trade-weighted won index is 34 percent weaker than its 1996 peak and is still about 30 percent below its levels just before the financial crisis struck in 2007.\par \par \uc2  Japan would be forced to go along, although no doubt it and all other Asian countries would reserve the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in extreme situations.\par \par \uc2  But the G7/IMF weight of opinion would persuade them that the current rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not extreme but a reflection of the relative strength of Asian economies in comparison to the developed world.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy has already baffled market participants. Tokyo confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Sept. 15, but has not provided any confirmation since. That leaves markets wondering, in the absence of any steer from officials, if there is a strategy.\par \par \uc2  Even without a strong G7 statement against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the strategy has been questioned by some within the Japanese government.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to continue to pressure the Bank of Japan for more policy action, as the announcement earlier this week of a new 5 trillion yen fund to buy bonds caused no more than a short-term blip in the yen <JPY=>.\par \par \uc2  The government also appears to be getting a little more creative lately. It announced it would use reserves to invest in the resource sector as well as other countries' bonds -- Japan may be taking a leaf out of China's book in this regard.\par \par \uc2  The MOF and BOJ focus on easing policies and diversification of reserves will cause the yen to underperform other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if and when they are allowed to appreciate.\par \par \uc2  We may even get a reiteration of the strong dollar policy from the United States this weekend.\par \par \uc2  It may only be a half-hearted commitment to maintain the dollar's strength, as they use every tool possible to revive the sluggish economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /ASIA (COLUMN)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|J|Z|UKI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101008e6a8000md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
