\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-BOJ mins: some warned on boosting fund-supply tool\b0\par\par\uc2 478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2010\par 02:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click)\par \par \uc2  *Board member Suda played down easing effects -  Aug mins\par \par \uc2  *Some members concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact on prices - Sept mins\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Some Bank of Japan policy board members warned about the adverse effects of expanding its cheap fund-supply tool, minutes from an Aug. 30 emergency meeting showed on Friday, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be reluctant to enlarge the scheme as part of any further monetary easing.\par \par \uc2  The minutes also showed that some members said the BOJ needed to act pre-emptively in case downside risks materialised in the U.S. and European economies.\par \par \uc2  At the Aug. 30 meeting, the BOJ boosted the size of its fixed-rate fund supply \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 30 trillion yen ($364.3 billion) from 20 trillion yen, bowing to government pressure for action to protect a fragile recovery by curbing the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2  The decision was by an 8-1 vote, with board member Miyako Suda dissenting.\par \par \uc2  "Some members noted the possibility that the expansion of the fixed-rate \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  might undermine the proper functioning of the market and reduce the bank's ability to control the overnight call rate," the minutes said.\par \par \uc2  The BOJ earlier this week surprised markets by cutting rates and vowing to buy 5 trillion yen worth of assets to provide fresh economic stimulus. It did not boost the size of the fixed-rate loan tool as some analysts had speculated.\par \par \uc2  Suda said that easing effects from expanding the fund-supply tool should be limited, the minutes also showed, but some members argued that there was still room for interest rates to go down.\par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's steps and yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month by the government has done little to halt the yen's advance, with the dollar hitting a new 15-year low against the yen on rising expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve will take aggressive easing steps.\par \par \uc2  Some analysts say the BOJ may eventually revert to a full-blown quantitative easing, though such a move could add to growing global tensions over competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation and easing by central banks.\par \par \uc2  How to nip a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war in the bud will top the agenda for world leaders at the Group of Seven and IMF meetings starting on Friday.\par \par \uc2  Underscoring the BOJ's concerns about the yen's gains, many members said at the Sept. 6-7 monetary policy meeting they need to pay attention to the rising yen's impact in pushing down consumer prices, minutes from the meeting showed.\par \par \uc2  The BOJ stood pat on monetary policy but vowed timely action when needed at the meeting.  (Reporting by Rie Ishiguro; Editing by Edmund Klamann and Nathan Layne)      \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/BOJ-MINUTES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101008e6a80000d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
