\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Recovers; Investors Cautious On US Jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 809 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2010\par 22:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar recovered from a broad slump against most of its rivals Thursday as investors pared bets on riskier assets ahead of the closely watched reading of monthly U.S. employment figures due Friday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar early Thursday dropped to a 15-year low against the yen, a record low against the Swiss franc and its lowest level since 1983 against the Australian dollar. As U.S. stocks took a turn lower, the dollar recovered much of its loss.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Friday's report on U.S. nonfarm payrolls, considered a key gauge of the pace of the economy, investors took some money off the risk table, helping the dollar, which is seen as a safe harbor, gain, though the greenback remains broadly weakened against its rivals, having fallen around 10% against the euro since July.\par \par \uc2 "Clients are hesitant to push too much" on the euro and other higher-yielding assets, said Amelia Bourdeau, senior G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2  in Stamford, Conn.\par \par \uc2 Late Thursday, the euro was at $1.3912 from $1.3929 late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose as high as $1.4030. The dollar was at Y82.40 from Y82.96, after falling as low as Y82.11, while the euro was at Y114.65 from Y115.55. The U.K. pound was at $1.5862 from $1.5885. The dollar was at CHF0.9669 from CHF0.9618.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 77.464 from 77.435, rebounding from a dip below 77, its lowest level since January.\par \par \uc2 Still, investors continue to expect a fresh round of stimulus from the Federal Reserve just around the corner, with the broad trend of dollar weakness likely to remain in place, said Steven Barrow, head of G10 strategy at Standard Bank in London.\par \par \uc2 While investors continue to speculate that a Fed stimulus program is imminent, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet, on the other hand, articulated a steady-on approach to monetary policy at the ECB's Thursday press conference; the ECB earlier left key rates unchanged. This contrast--the ECB on the path to eventual policy normalization, with the Fed possibly near to policy loosening--propelled the euro above $1.40.\par \par \uc2 To see the euro's performance against the dollar, please see:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4701"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4701}}}\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar took advantage of broad dollar weakness and a much better-than-expected Australian jobs report by shooting to its highest level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1983, gaining above the US$0.99 mark, leading some analysts to point to possible parity. The U.S. dollar took back some of the Aussie's gains as U.S. stocks dipped into the red. By afternoon in New York, the Australian dollar was at $0.9818 from $0.9774 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Before posting a gain against the Swiss franc, the dollar earlier fell to a new all-time low against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dropping as low as CHF0.9555, while the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also declined against the yen, dropping to the fresh 15-year low, at Y82.11, and keeping investors on alert for signs of Japan in the market to prop the dollar and stem yen strength.\par \par \uc2 Hidetoshi Yanagihara, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York, said there were no signs of Japan in the market to stem yen strength.\par \par \uc2 Investors still think \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible, but they said the risk is decreasing for now because a meeting of financial ministers and central bankers from the Group of Seven industrialized nations will be held this weekend. Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  just before the meeting would raise difficult questions for Japanese authorities in trying to explain that they aren't just pushing the yen lower to gain a trade advantage against other nations.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of England also left its monetary policy unchanged Thursday, though speculation mounted whether the bank's Monetary Policy Committee would eventually enact another round of its own stimulus--asset purchases dubbed quantitative easing--which would likely weigh on the pound. The U.K. pound was down by about 0.3% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 With the ICE Dollar Index strengthening slightly, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bearish exchange-traded fund was down 0.15% from late Wednesday, while its PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bullish was up 0.13%. The two exchange-traded funds are based on \uc2 Deutsche Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -futures indexes, whose composition mirrors that of the ICE's Dollar Index.\par \par \uc2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654; bradley.davis@dowjones.com [ 10-07-10 1609ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101007e6a7000db\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
