\par\par \b \uc2 Nikkei slips on yen strength; US jobs data awaited\b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2010\par 01:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 * Nikkei down 1 pct on yen, profit-taking; technicals strong\par \par \uc2 * Nikkei books best week since mid-September, up 2 pct\par \par \uc2 * Yen hurts but BOJ steps continue to support - fund manager\par \par \uc2 * Focus on prospects for G7, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Aiko Hayashi and Chikafumi Hodo\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Japan's Nikkei average fell 1 percent on Friday, hurt by the yen trading near a 15-year peak against the dollar and by profit-taking after the Bank of Japan's policy easing this week had driven stocks higher.\par \par \uc2 Investors were also keen to unwind positions ahead of key U.S. payroll data later in the day, which may provide clues as to whether the Federal Reserve will resume quantitative easing, and ahead of a three-day weekend in Japan.\par \par \uc2 Despite its softness on Friday, the Nikkei gained 2 percent on the week, its best weekly performance since mid-September, as investor confidence improved after the BOJ on Tuesday cut interest rates to virtually zero and pledged to pump more funds into the struggling economy.\par \par \uc2 "The market faced pressure as the BOJ's steps haven't proven to be really effective on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, with the yen remaining on the strong side ahead of the U.S. jobs data and due to speculation for quantitative easing by the Fed," said Junichi Misawa, senior fund manager at STB Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 "But policy hopes, which had been almost non-existent until the BOJ's announcement of its rather bold steps, are providing support to the stock market."\par \par \uc2 The potential for yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a Group of Seven nations meeting this weekend was also a key focus for the market, as its outcome could influence views on when or whether Japanese officials will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to pull down the yen.\par \par \uc2 "The market is watching to see if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Group of Seven meeting to prevent further firming of the yen," said Yutaka Miura, senior technical analyst at Mizuho Securities.\par \par \uc2 "If the yen advances more and Wall Street falls after the G7, then the Nikkei would be hit very hard."\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Nikkei ended the day down 95.93 points at 9,588.88, speeding up its fall as it headed into the close.\par \par \uc2 The broader Topix fell 0.8 percent to 839.44.\par \par \uc2 The yen stood at 82.38 against the dollar, not far away from a 15-year high of 82.11 yen reached the previous day.\par \par \uc2 Caution over possible Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased since the yen rose beyond 82.87 -- the level where Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in six years on Sept. 15.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. non-farm payrolls report is expected to show payrolls were unchanged in September, an outcome that would cement expectations of further Federal Reserve action to spur the recovery.\par \par \uc2 Many market players think expectations of quantitative easing by the Fed will keep pushing the dollar lower.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's next policy-making meeting is scheduled for Nov. 2 and 3.\par \par \uc2 After the close, \uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2  forecast a 14.3 percent fall in annual operating profit this business year, as sales at its Uniqlo casual clothing chain lose steam. The stock had ended the day down 2.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 BULLISH TECHNICALS\par \par \uc2 Although the Nikkei edged lower, market participants said technical sentiment had turned bullish especially after breaking through several chart points this week.\par \par \uc2 The 25-day moving average of 9,411 and the 75-day average of 9,399 have become major technical support levels.\par \par \uc2 "The Nikkei may be under downward pressure, but there is plenty of demand to buy on dips based on strong technical trends," said Hiroichi Nishi, general manager of equity marketing at Nikko Cordial Securities.\par \par \uc2 Property stocks ran out of steam after posting strong gains this week on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan to set up a $60 billion fund to buy a wide range of assets, including Japanese real estate investment trust (J-REITs).\par \par \uc2 Mitsubishi Estate lost 1.3 percent to 1,489 yen, but has gained about 7 percent since the BOJ news.\par \par \uc2 Exporters fell hurt by the yen as the strong home \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eats into their earnings when repatriated and curbs their competitiveness overseas.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo Electron Ltd\uc2  slipped 2 percent to 4,575 yen and \uc2 Canon Inc\uc2  fell 1.2 percent to 3,830 yen.\par \par \uc2 Seven & I Holdings\uc2  fell 3.7 percent to 1,975 yen after Japan's largest retailer kept its annual forecasts unchanged due to weakness at its large retail outlets, disappointing investors hoping government stimulus efforts would improve its outlook.\par \par \uc2 But banking shares added to gains made after the announcement of the BOJ's easing news. Japan's top lender \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group\uc2  inched up 0.3 percent to 406 yen, bringing its gains since the news to about 6 percent.\par \par \uc2 Some 1.97 billion shares changed hands on the Tokyo exchange's first section, down from a five-month high of 2.88 billion booked on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Declining stocks outnumbered advancing ones by more than 2 to 1. (Editing by Chris Gallagher)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-JAPAN-STOCKS (UPDATE 5)|LANGEN|Table|ABX|BNX|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101007e6a7001pi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
